# profile: ollama
# @tier: 1
# @summary: Everything local: chat and embeddings on an Ollama server. No account, no key, no network.
# @key: none. Start the server with a raised context: OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=64000 ollama serve
#   Then: ollama pull qwen2.5:14b && ollama pull nomic-embed-text
# @cost: free (your hardware)
# @dotnet: yes
# @verified: Ollama and a two-tool loop on qwen2.5:14b, gemma4:12b and qwen3.5:9b were tried by hand in 2026-08
#   (see .env.example). The capability probes also ran on qwen2.5:7b (tools, parallel calls, streaming and tool
#   results passed, a forced tool_choice did not). The 768-dimension embedding path is documented, not
#   exercised. Not run in CI.
# @evals: live quality and safety suites through the eval CLI, capability check. Expect lower scores than a hosted
#   model: that is the measurement, not a bug. Cost is null (unpriced); add a 0 entry to a pricing overrides file to show 0.
# @judge: a local model should not grade itself. Suggestion only, not calibrated (D-7, M3).
# @judge-env: JUDGE_PROVIDER=openai JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-5.1
# Host URLs below; dev.sh rewrites localhost to host.docker.internal for the containers.
# nomic-embed-text is 768-wide and the database column is 1536: dev.sh runs
# scripts/reset_embeddings.py --if-needed --dim 768 once. Until you run `python -m scripts.generate_embeddings`
# semantic search uses full-text only.
LLM_PROVIDER=openai
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
LLM_API=chat_completions
LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b
OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
EMBEDDING_API_KEY=ollama
EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
EMBEDDING_DIM=768
